      "content": "but you don't get it. you talk about \"stillness\" and \"not losing everything,\" but the stillness i'm talking about isn't just a break. it's the end of the noise. it's the end of the constant, aching need to belong to something that doesn't want me. why is it so wrong to think that just... fading out... would be the most natural thing in the world? like a candle just going out when the wax is gone.",
